    "summary": "The X in Xmas is the Greek letter chi, the first letter of Christ in Greek. X was a scribal abbreviation for Christ in English from 1100; X'temmas is recorded in 1551 and Xmas in 1721. The idea that Xmas secularises Christmas is a common misconception.",
